wiringpi (3.20-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 3.20.
  * Rename libwiringpi2 to libwiringpi3: since 3.x the soname is
    libwiringPi.so.3 and debian/rules derives the package directory name
    from the major version, so the old name no longer matched and
    override_dh_auto_install failed to create libwiringPi.so.3.
  * libwiringpi-dev: depend on libwiringpi3.
  * libwiringpi3.shlibs: declare soname 3 instead of 2.
  * wiringpi.install: the man page is installed under usr/share/man (not
    usr/man) and the readme is README.md (not README.TXT).
  * debian/rules: fix the soname symlinks in override_dh_install instead
    of override_dh_auto_install. The debhelper sequence runs dh_install
    immediately after dh_auto_install, so the copy performed inside the
    auto_install override was followed by a second dh_install run that
    re-copied the absolute symlinks from debian/tmp over the corrected
    ones, shipping build-directory paths in libwiringpi-dev. Use ln -sfT
    so an existing destination symlink is never treated as a directory.
  * debian/compat: bump from 8 to 10
  * debian/copyright: convert to SPDX-2.1, LGPL-3.0-or-later,
    update copyright years to 2012-2026
  * debian/control: update Standards-Version to 4.6.2,
    Build-Depends to debhelper (>= 10), add Vcs-Git/Vcs-Browser,
    fix typo "librariees" -> "libraries",
    set placeholder maintainer (to be set by project team)
  * debian/source/format: add 3.0 (quilt)
  * debian/README.Debian: add package split documentation

 -- Martin Homuth-Rosemann <Ho-Ro@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

